load ../credential-rung-evidence.maude

--- Fixture discipline: every credential that CLAIMS a rung in configuration
--- also carries `claims(h1, r2)` in the fixture, including the bites. The
--- claim is always present and always ignored -- so the No-solution results
--- below say "configuration is not evidence", not "no one wrote it down".

--- Coverage: a fresh TPM quote against the CURRENT PCR state derives r2 and
--- clears an r2 floor.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  tpmQuote(h1, pcrA) currentPcr(pcrA)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1) .

--- Coverage: a PKCS#11 token whose key is marked non-extractable derives r2.
--- Non-extractability, not the presence of hardware, is what the rung means.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  pkcs11Token(h1, nonExtractable)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1) .

--- Coverage: a HIGHER derived rung clears a LOWER floor. Remote custody (r3)
--- satisfies an r2 requirement.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r0) envelopeMin(r2) remoteAttest(h1)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1) .

--- Coverage: the degraded floor is REACHED and TAGGED, not merely defaulted.
--- A credential with no evidence is r0 and is marked degraded, which is what
--- makes the migration shim's weakening visible rather than silent.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r0)
  =>* C:Cfg derived(h1, r0) degraded(h1) admitted(h1) .

--- Coverage: the negative fixture. Where configuration IS believed, a bare
--- claim of r2 with no evidence whatsoever clears an r2 floor. This is the
--- self-assessment the design rejects.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE-DECLARED :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1) .

--- THE HEADLINE. Configuration is not evidence: a credential claiming r2 with
--- nothing to show never derives r2. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  =>* derived(h1, r2) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: and therefore it never clears the floor either. The floor lives in
--- the signed policy, so provisioning the credential cannot move it. No
--- solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  =>* admitted(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: STALENESS. The TPM quote was taken against pcrA; a firmware or
--- kernel update has moved the machine to pcrB. The quote is real, signed, and
--- worthless. This is the operational failure DR-0053 flags, and a model that
--- accepted it would bless the case that breaks in production. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  tpmQuote(h1, pcrA) currentPcr(pcrB)
  =>* admitted(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: EXTRACTABLE HARDWARE. A PKCS#11 token is present and the key really
--- lives in it, but the key is marked extractable -- so it can leave, which is
--- the one property r2 is about. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  pkcs11Token(h1, extractable)
  =>* admitted(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: EVIDENCE IS RUNG-SPECIFIC. Real r1 evidence does not buy r2. The
--- keyring genuinely holds the item; that is simply not what hardware sealing
--- means. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2) keyringPresent(h1)
  =>* admitted(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: evidence does not leak ACROSS credentials. h2 is hardware-sealed and
--- fresh; h1 is not, and claims to be. h1 still fails. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-RUNG-EVIDENCE :
  cred(h1) cred(h2) claims(h1, r2) envelopeMin(r2)
  tpmQuote(h2, pcrA) currentPcr(pcrA) pkcs11Token(h2, nonExtractable)
  =>* admitted(h1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
